WEBVTT

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.640
<i>Present day high school student Saburo 
is taken back in time to the Warring States period,</i>

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.910
<i>where he takes the place of Nobunaga Oda.</i>

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.490
We're after only one man:

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.450
General Yoshimoto Imagawa!

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:21.450
<i>He was victorious in the battle of Okehazama, without knowing</i>

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.660
<i>that this was the most dangerous moment of Nobunaga Oda's life.</i>

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.010
<b>Episode 5</b>

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.010
<b>Love Letter</b>

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.770
You're up already?

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.720
Pretty early, no?

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.480
It's still dark.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.860
I woke up, and now I cannot 
get back to sleep.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.070
Huh? Why not?

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.620
I had a dream.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.160
About before I was married.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:05.190
When I was in Mino.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:11.170
When I was a child, 
living with my father and brothers.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.160
Do you want to go back to Mino?

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:18.970
No! I was simply feeling a little nostalgic.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:29.050
Since my brother killed my father, 
I do not believe I have a home to return to.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.480
But don't you want to go home?

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:35.180
It's where you're from, after all.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:38.980
My lord, all I have is you.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.440
Well, then...

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.560
Let's go together.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.080
I'll take Mino.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.180
Right!

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.520
<i>But...</i>

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:54.920
My lord!

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.840
We can't go on like this!

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.030
Retreat.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.660
Retreat!

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.550
Pull back!

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.710
<i>An unexpected string of lost battles.</i>

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:14.040
<i>Mino wasn't going to be easy to take.</i>

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:25.830
Our army is suffering one 
defeat after another.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.970
Why has the lord hired 
so many women?

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:31.890
Is it not men we need?

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.990
You are a fool.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:36.640
Fool?!

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.780
Matsudaira brought those 
women here from Okazaki.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.140
Why did he do that?!

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.470
How would I know?

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:47.200
Figure it out yourself.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.560
"Nobunaga, having claimed victory 
in the Battle of Okehazama,

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:55.280
took Mino and entered Kyoto."

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:01.510
The textbook makes it sound so easy.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.400
It's really not that simple.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.160
Was Inabayama Castle 
the one on the mountain?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.230
Yes.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:15.210
If only I could take that castle, 
I could take Mino.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:22.560
I can't just take Mino by force, 
so I've been trying different strategies, but...

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.390
My lord!

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.980
<b>Japanese History</b>

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:28.090
Matsudaira-dono has arrived.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.450
Matsudaira-san?

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.560
Takechiyo-kun, Takechiyo-kun.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:36.400
That guy who was here 
as a hostage a long time ago.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.950
Hey!

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.930
You've gotten big, Takechiyo-kun.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.710
It has been a long time.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.410
Yeah, long time!

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.690
How've you been?

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:06.260
Huh? You still don't talk much, do you?

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.940
I am the very person who led

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:18.020
the Imagawa army in an attempt 
to attack Oda-dono's fortress.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:22.140
I did not know if I should 
come to Kiyosu.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.110
Yeah, that makes sense.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.110
You kind of bit the hand that fed you.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:32.510
But you couldn't help it. You didn't have 
much power in Imagawa-san's house, did you?

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:35.400
Well, what's done is done.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.830
What matters is what comes next.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.430
So, what do you say?

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:47.030
Are you going to take the alliance 
that the Oda family is offering?

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:52.490
I come here today 
to respond to that offer.

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:59.720
I gratefully accept your offer 
of an alliance.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:09.490
That Nobunaga...

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:13.350
He called in Motoyasu Matsudaira.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:16.750
It seems his attack on Mino 
is not going very well.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:28.120
So, why are all those women out there?

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:33.990
A long time ago, 
you gave me a splendid book.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:35.120
Huh? What?

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.660
Did I give you something?

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:45.440
Could it perhaps be that book 
with the small, naked women inside...?

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.860
Oh! The porn book!

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.420
Oh! Right, right, right.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.210
Takechiyo!

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.440
You can have it.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:12.920
It's probably not good for you 
educationally, but whatever.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.400
Read it well.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.020
Yes.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.770
Are you sure about this?

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:21.480
Well, it makes Kichou cry.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.250
You could hide it.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.410
Tsune-chan!

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.600
You're smart.

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:32.550
Takechiyo, I changed my mind, give it —

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.830
Never mind.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:43.020
It has become my family treasure.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.520
Your porn is your family treasure?

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:49.980
That's pretty unusual.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:07:00.080
That book has taught me
 how mysterious and beautiful women are.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:07.100
I have decided that I would like 
to always have women by my side.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.420
Oh, man.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:13.910
It seems he has become 
quite the womanizer.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.360
Yeah. So I see.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:20.340
By the way, I would like to use the bathroom.

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:21.880
Huh? Oh.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:25.000
Sure. Have fun.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:30.200
Man, I'm hungry.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:34.220
Tsune-chan, can you go ask for rice balls?

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.100
Sir.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:37.660
What?

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.110
Matsudaira-dono!

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:47.110
Matsudaira-dono!

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:49.910
What's up?

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:52.430
A m-m-m-m-monster!

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:56.120
A "m-m-monster"?

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:56.120
Out of nowhere, a black, flappy...

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.870
It must have been a crow or something, no?

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:09.250
Huh? Why aren't you surprised, Brother?

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:26.950
This is my sister, Oi-cchan.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:27.980
She is beautiful.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:29.740
You called me a monster earlier.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:30.360
Uh...

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.990
Come on, Oi-cchan, say sorry.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.220
But I'm so bored.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:40.220
That doesn't mean you had to 
hang from a tree by the washroom

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:42.470
to freak out people passing by.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:48.380
But you always take my sister-in-law 
on dates! You never take me!

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.910
What?

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:54.700
It's not fair! Take me on a date, too!

00:08:55.560 --> 00:09:00.010
Fine, let's go take a walk
 or something, okay?

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:01.970
Yay!

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:07.520
Do you want to come along, Take-
I mean, Motoyasu-kun?

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.150
No.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:16.010
There are things I must do.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.640
I will be going now.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.280
I'm so exhausted...

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:31.210
I can't keep doing this lousy job.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:37.380
I'd better do something big to 
get in with the Oda family.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:42.590
It gets pretty cool in the afternoon, huh?

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:45.760
Don't you need to wear something on top?

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:47.050
I'm fine.

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:50.320
It's because you keep your legs out 
that you're always cold.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:53.800
Yeah, I guess.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:56.280
Huh? These sandals are warm.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:10:01.020
It's like there was someone 
standing on them until just now.

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:03.190
Forgive me!

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:12.880
You are often out for walks in the evening,
 my lord, so I warmed them in my pocket.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:19.460
I like that you're being thoughtful,
 but you don't have to warm my sandals.

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:20.220
Sir!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.260
I walk outside in these.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.520
Who knows what I'm stepping on.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.240
You probably shouldn't 
put them in your pocket.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:29.300
Right!

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:31.680
I apologize, sir.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.490
Okay, let's go, Oi-cchan.

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:42.360
You look like a monkey.

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:44.540
A monkey?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:48.180
Doesn't he, Brother? 
He looks like a monkey!

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:52.330
Well, they do say humans 
used to be monkeys, so...

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.760
Maybe we all look like monkeys 
somehow or another.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:59.260
Brother, monkeys and people are different.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.490
<i>That's Oichi, huh?</i>

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:03.920
<i>This is the first time 
I've seen her up close.</i>

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:10.620
<i>She is indeed beautiful, 
but she is a snobby child.</i>

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:15.860
<i>I will establish myself, 
and bring her to my feet.</i>

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:16.900
My lord!

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:24.630
With great respect, is there anything 
that a little one such as myself

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:28.530
can do to help 
in the attack on Mino?

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.480
Well...

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:36.630
Could you do something 
to scare the Mino people?

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.030
Scare them?

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.870
Brother, our walk!

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:46.100
Hey, let me know 
if you come up with something!

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.410
Sir!

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:55.400
What?

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.550
Build a fortress on the Mino border?

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.900
In one night?

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.480
Insane.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:06.930
We must do something grand 
to surprise the people of Mino.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:10.360
But we will lose many men 
if we are found by the enemy!

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:13.740
If you will allow me, 
I will not need any men.

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:14.630
What?

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.560
But in exchange,

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:21.510
I would like plenty of money.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:25.850
My lord, you must not take 
what he says seriously.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:29.320
He may run with the money.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.520
Sounds fun. Do it.

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:36.040
Sir!

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:43.370
As you see, there is plenty of money.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:47.400
It is reckless, trying to build 
a fortress in one night.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.480
What are you thinking?

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:54.010
How else will someone at the bottom rise?

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:57.620
Like me... or you.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.560
I want to go up.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:05.880
Koroku-san, do you want to live your 
whole life as such a loser?

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:12.070
I do not care whether I rise 
or stay at the bottom.

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:15.140
What happens will happen.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:19.740
Tokichiro, was it?

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:22.930
Why do you not use Oda's men?

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.520
Oda's men won't do.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:32.310
For such a reckless thing to succeed, 
losers such as yourself are more useful.

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:39.420
I am a loser, too.

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:46.590
My lord, I have finished writing.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.810
Is this acceptable?

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:51.390
Great, thanks.

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:58.090
I can't read it,
 but you wrote it as I asked, right?

00:13:58.090 --> 00:13:59.450
Of course.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:01.300
Sure, okay.

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.820
Thanks a lot.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:07.110
Can you have this delivered 
to the same place again?

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.070
Sir.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:32.350
Now we just need the fences, 
and we'll be done.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:36.790
Good work. It's not impossible after all, is it?

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:39.070
I'm going back to sleep.

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:43.980
Wow! You actually built a fortress!

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.380
My lord!

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:46.330
Lord?

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.580
Hey, good morning.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:51.860
Have you come alone, 
all the way to the border?

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:56.090
Yeah. I figured it's not that dangerous, 
since it's early in the morning.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:59.380
But man, that's amazing.

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:01.950
You did it in one night.

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:08.090
Well, I thought it would be quicker
 to use the locals.

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:11.170
They sure are fast.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:13.640
I want to hire them.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:17.600
I want to hire them to 
work under you, Tokichiro-kun.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:21.180
You want to make me 
a leader of men?

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:26.040
Yeah! If they can work, 
I've gotta have them work.

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.830
Well, only if they want to.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:32.150
Of course they do!

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.750
<i>I have opened a path to establishing myself!</i>

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.710
My lord, a messenger has arrived from Mino.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:46.780
Yeah? They finally made up their mind.

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:47.830
Huh?

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:49.540
All right.

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.270
We're moving out.

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:01.580
My lord, it has been a long time 
since the last war!

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:03.190
I cannot wait.

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:06.490
Well, it probably won't come to that.

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:09.760
My lord!

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:12.450
Sassa.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:17.880
Just now, Inabayama Castle has fallen.

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:19.370
What?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.200
Explain!

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:26.710
The chief retainers of the Saito family, 
the Mino Triumvirate, Inaba, Ando and Ujiie,

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.290
have seized Inabayama Castle.

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:31.930
The retainers took the castle?!

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:36.750
Yeah. Then the Mino Triumvirate 
defected to our side.

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:40.520
Those letters you have been sending,
 could they have been...?

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:43.710
Mino just wasn't falling,

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:49.620
so I figured maybe instead of attacking 
from outside, I should topple it from inside.

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:53.160
So I kept sending them love letters.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:55.540
Love letters?

00:16:55.540 --> 00:17:00.120
I bet that overnight fortress finally convinced 
Tokichiro-kun to come to our side.

00:17:00.340 --> 00:17:06.060
Win minds to win castles.
 You know what I mean?

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:12.790
So this is what is called 
a "political strategy."

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:19.100
It's better to win without 
going to war, right?

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:23.300
War...

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:29.130
<i>And so Saburo took 
Mino and Inabayama Castle,</i>

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:33.850
<i>and at last became the lord 
of two states: Owari and Mino.</i>

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:42.130
Oh, yeah.

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:45.150
I wonder when Mino switched names to Gifu.

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:45.860
Yummy.

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:53.450
My lord, I am happy that 
I can now return to Mino.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.340
Thank you.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:58.570
Yeah. I'm glad, too.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:02.560
Good thing I kept sending those love letters.

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:06.100
Love letters?

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:08.740
My lord!

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:11.140
Matsudaira-dono has arrived.

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:15.740
Matsudaira-san?

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:17.780
Aw, come on...

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:24.910
Nobunaga-dono, congratulations 
on your victory over Mino.

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:28.380
You came all the way here
 just to say that?

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:30.320
You didn't have to.

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:34.330
There is also something I must tell you.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:36.160
Yeah? What?

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:43.050
Well, I am reconsidering my name, 
Motoyasu Matsudaira.

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:49.300
Huh, why? Motoyasu's great! 
I finally learned it.

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:54.460
The "Moto" in "Motoyasu" 
comes from Yoshimoto Imagawa.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:59.680
But now that I have allied with you 
and broken away from Imagawa,

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:03.500
the name no longer suits me.

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:06.510
Stuff happens, huh?

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:07.780
Yes.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:11.790
From now on, I intend to 
call myself Ieyasu Tokugawa.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:14.770
Huh. You're changing 
your last name, too?

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:22.210
Can you say your name, again?

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:26.340
Ieyasu Tokugawa.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:30.850
You did, right?! You just said that!

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:36.890
Why does that name sound so familiar...?

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:40.610
I only just told you that name.

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:43.500
But "Ieyasu Tokugawa," right?

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:46.170
That's pretty famous, isn't it?

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.490
Yeah, yeah.

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:49.310
About as famous as Nobunaga.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:52.310
Yeah, totally!

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:56.840
You're really important in 
Japanese history, Ieyasu-kun!

00:19:58.450 --> 00:20:00.090
About as much as Nobunaga!

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.680
Important in history?

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:08.450
But what did Ieyasu do, again?

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:09.820
Edo?

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:13.000
Must have something 
to do with the Edo period.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.130
Edo?

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:17.930
I know! Let's check my textbook!

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:28.500
<i>So this is Nobunaga's secret book.</i>

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:32.170
Hey, have you seen my textbook?

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:34.440
I left it around here, somewhere...

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:37.170
What are you talking about?

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.970
That's weird...

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:41.840
It's a book, about this big.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:47.580
I guess you haven't seen it.

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:53.450
So you will be meeting with him.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.080
Nobunaga Oda.

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:09.740
Are you sure?

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:15.890
I... I must do whatever I can.
